## Summary

Port the Hysteria v2.14.0 UDP forwarding optimization
(HyNetworks/hysteria@c2b181e) to `proxy/hysteria`. The wire format is
unchanged; this only removes per-packet allocations.

Refs: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/issues/7484

## Changes

- `ParseUDPMessage` reads the fixed header in place with `quicvarint.Parse`
  instead of `bytes.Buffer` and `binary.Read`.
- `UDPReader` parses into a reused packet buffer and message, and keeps the
  last address string and its parsed destination. Each packet still gets its
  own `*net.Destination`: freedom and the endpoint override rewrite `b.UDP` in
  place. Fragment data is cloned, as `Defragger` keeps fragments between reads.
- `UDPWriter` caches the last `b.UDP` and its `NetAddr`, and finds
  `*quic.DatagramTooLargeError` with `errors.AsType`.
- Update `apernet/quic-go` to v0.65.1 (the version used by Hysteria v2.14.0)
  and adapt MASQUE CONNECT-IP to `HTTPStream()` returning an error.

## Benchmarks

1200 B datagram, Go 1.27.4, linux/amd64, Intel Core Ultra 7 266V (8 threads),
`-count=10`, benchstat medians, all p=0.000. `old` is `b56ffef3` with the same
quic-go.

| Path | Allocs/op | B/op | Time |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| `ParseUDPMessage` | 7 → 2 | 120 → 64 | 180 → 69 ns |
| `UDPWriter.WriteMultiBuffer` | 5 → 2 | 112 → 72 | 212 → 140 ns |
| `UDPReader.ReadFrom` | 12 → 1 | 1724 → 24 | 1231 → 66 ns |
| `UDPReader.ReadMultiBuffer` | 15 → 4 | 1804 → 104 | 1550 → 252 ns |

The writer itself no longer allocates; both remaining allocations are
`buf.New` and `Buffer.Release` in the benchmark loop. The one `ReadFrom`
allocation is the per-packet `*net.Destination`; `ReadMultiBuffer` adds three
from `common/buf`.

<details>
<summary>Benchmark</summary>

```go
package hysteria

import (
	"io"
	"testing"

	"github.com/xtls/xray-core/common/buf"
	xnet "github.com/xtls/xray-core/common/net"
)

const benchAddr = "203.0.113.1:53"

func benchDatagram() []byte {
	m := &UDPMessage{PacketID: 1, FragCount: 1, Addr: benchAddr, Data: make([]byte, 1200)}
	b := make([]byte, m.Size())
	return b[:m.Serialize(b)]
}

// repeatReader returns the same datagram on every Read.
type repeatReader struct{ datagram []byte }

func (r *repeatReader) Read(p []byte) (int, error) { return copy(p, r.datagram), nil }

func BenchmarkParseUDPMessage(b *testing.B) {
	msg := benchDatagram()
	b.ReportAllocs()
	for b.Loop() {
		if _, err := ParseUDPMessage(msg); err != nil {
			b.Fatal(err)
		}
	}
}

func BenchmarkUDPWriterWriteMultiBuffer(b *testing.B) {
	dest := xnet.UDPDestination(xnet.ParseAddress("203.0.113.1"), 53)
	payload := make([]byte, 1200)
	w := &UDPWriter{writer: io.Discard, addr: benchAddr}
	mb := make(buf.MultiBuffer, 1)
	b.ReportAllocs()
	for b.Loop() {
		mb[0] = buf.New()
		mb[0].Write(payload)
		mb[0].UDP = &dest
		if err := w.WriteMultiBuffer(mb); err != nil {
			b.Fatal(err)
		}
	}
}

func BenchmarkUDPReaderReadFrom(b *testing.B) {
	r := &UDPReader{reader: &repeatReader{benchDatagram()}, df: &Defragger{}}
	p := make([]byte, buf.Size)
	b.ReportAllocs()
	for b.Loop() {
		if _, _, err := r.ReadFrom(p); err != nil {
			b.Fatal(err)
		}
	}
}

func BenchmarkUDPReaderReadMultiBuffer(b *testing.B) {
	r := &UDPReader{reader: &repeatReader{benchDatagram()}, df: &Defragger{}}
	b.ReportAllocs()
	for b.Loop() {
		mb, err := r.ReadMultiBuffer()
		if err != nil {
			b.Fatal(err)
		}
		buf.ReleaseMulti(mb)
	}
}
```

</details>

## Compatibility

The Hysteria wire format does not change. Old and new Xray builds and
official Hysteria v2.14.0 peers remain interoperable. No config or API
changes.

